// Guns (lane GEOMETRY, card C-004), original designs in the proportions of the classes they are named for; nothing is quoted from memory.
// Metres. Frame of a gun: the trunnion axis through the origin, the bore along -Z, +Y up. Provenance ESTIMATE for every number, bands +-25%.
//   receiver_m      width (x), height (y), length (z) of the receiver box, centred on the bore
//   pivot_back_frac the share of the receiver length that lies behind the trunnion axis
//   barrel_len_m    from the receiver's front face to the muzzle device
//   jacket          (length, radius) of the thicker shroud over the root of the barrel
//   muzzle_m        (length, radius) of the muzzle device (flash hider or brake)
//   ammo            boxes: size (x, y, z), centre (x, y, z) of the right-hand one, and whether it has a left-hand twin
//   grips           a cross-bar behind the receiver (radius, half span) with a handle at each end (x, radius, drop below the bar)
//   sight           size of an optics block on the roof of the receiver, its z from the trunnion axis
//   overlap_m       parts that join overlap by this much, so nothing floats
